{"id":"120142598662395fc45286fbbb3afdc4203b3e13","axis":"silent","repo":"pnpm/pnpm","sha":"120142598662395fc45286fbbb3afdc4203b3e13","parsed":{"files":[{"path":".changeset/repeat-install-skips-unchanged-manifests.md","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@","+---","+\"pacquet\": patch","+---","+","+`pnpm install` in a workspace that is already up to date no longer reads the `package.json` of each project whose file did not change since the last install [pnpm/tasks#256](https://github.com/pnpm/tasks/issues/256)."],"additions":5,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpm/crates/cli/tests/suite/main.rs","lines":["@@ -173,6 +173,7 @@ mod remove;"," mod removed_overrides;"," mod repeat_install;"," mod repeat_install_oracle;","+mod repeat_install_records;"," mod repo;"," mod reporter_setting;"," mod restart;"],"additions":1,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpm/crates/cli/tests/suite/repeat_install_records.rs","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,338 @@","+//! The repeat-install fast path deciding from the workspace state's manifest","+//! records, without reading the project manifests whose recorded stat still","+//! holds.","+","+pub use _utils::*;","+","+use crate::_utils;","+","+use assert_cmd::prelude::*;","+use command_extra::CommandExtra;","+use pnpm_testing_utils::bin::{AddMockedRegistry, CommandTempCwd};","+use std::{fs, path::Path};","+","+/// The debug event the fast path logs when the records decided.","+const DECIDED_FROM_RECORDS: &str = \"the recorded manifests decided the install\";","+","+/// The span that reads the project manifests.","+const READ_PROJECTS_SPAN: &str = \"discover_workspace_projects\";","+","+/// A workspace whose `a` depends on `b` through `workspace:*` and links its","+/// command, beside a `packages/*` directory that holds no project.","+fn write_workspace(workspace: &Path) {","+    let workspace_yaml = workspace.join(\"pnpm-workspace.yaml\");","+    let mut yaml = fs::read_to_string(&workspace_yaml).expect(\"read pnpm-workspace.yaml\");","+    yaml.push_str(\"packages:\\n  - packages/*\\n\");","+    fs::write(&workspace_yaml, yaml).expect(\"write pnpm-workspace.yaml\");","+    let write_manifest = |dir: &str, manifest: serde_json::Value| {","+        fs::create_dir_all(workspace.join(dir)).expect(\"create the project directory\");","+        fs::write(workspace.join(dir).join(\"package.json\"), manifest.to_string())","+            .expect(\"write package.json\");","+    };","+    write_manifest(\".\", serde_json::json!({ \"name\": \"root\", \"private\": true }));","+    write_manifest(","+        \"packages/a\",","+        serde_json::json!({ \"name\": \"a\", \"version\": \"1.0.0\", \"dependencies\": { \"b\": \"workspace:*\" } }),","+    );","+    write_manifest(","+        \"packages/b\",","+        serde_json::json!({ \"name\": \"b\", \"version\": \"1.0.0\", \"bin\": { \"b\": \"cli.js\" } }),","+    );","+    fs::write(workspace.join(\"packages/b/cli.js\"), \"#!/usr/bin/env node\\n\").expect(\"write cli.js\");","+    fs::create_dir_all(workspace.join(\"packages/no-project\")).expect(\"create packages/no-project\");","+}","+","+/// On a filesystem that keeps whole seconds, a stat recorded within two","+/// seconds of the write is not trusted. There, wait past that window, so the","+/// next install records the stats trusted.","+fn wait_past_whole_second_rounding(workspace: &Path) {","+    let modified = fs::metadata(workspace.join(\"pnpm-lock.yaml\"))","+        .expect(\"stat the lockfile\")","+        .modified()","+        .expect(\"read the mtime\");","+    let whole_seconds = modified","+        .duration_since(std::time::UNIX_EPOCH)","+        .expect(\"an mtime after the epoch\")","+        .subsec_nanos()","+        == 0;","+    if whole_seconds {","+        std::thread::sleep(std::time::Duration::from_millis(2_100));","+    }","+}","+","+/// [`wait_past_whole_second_rounding`], then an install that records the","+/// stats again, so the records the next install reads are trusted.","+fn trust_recorded_stats(workspace: &Path, registry: &str) {","+    wait_past_whole_second_rounding(workspace);","+    pacquet_in(workspace)","+        .with_env(\"PNPM_CONFIG_REGISTRY\", registry)","+        .with_arg(\"install\")","+        .assert()","+        .success();","+}","+","+/// `pnpm install` with the fast path's trace, returning its output.","+fn traced_install(workspace: &Path, registry: &str) -> String {","+    let output = pacquet_in(workspace)","+        .with_env(\"PNPM_CONFIG_REGISTRY\", registry)","+        .with_env(\"TRACE\", \"pacquet::install=debug\")","+        .with_arg(\"install\")","+        .assert()","+        .success()","+        .get_output()","+        .clone();","+    format!(","+        \"{}{}\",","+        String::from_utf8_lossy(&output.stdout),","+        String::from_utf8_lossy(&output.stderr),","+    )","+}","+","+#[test]","+fn an_unchanged_workspace_is_up_to_date_from_the_records() {","+    let CommandTempCwd {","+        pacquet,","+        root,","+        workspace,","+        npmrc_info,","+        ..","+    } = CommandTempCwd::init().add_mocked_registry();","+    let AddMockedRegistry { mock_instance, .. } = npmrc_info;","+    write_workspace(&workspace);","+    pacquet","+        .with_env(\"PNPM_CONFIG_REGISTRY\", mock_instance.url())","+        .with_arg(\"install\")","+        .assert()","+        .success();","+    trust_recorded_stats(&workspace, mock_instance.url());","+","+    let output = traced_install(&workspace, mock_instance.url());","+","+    assert!(output.contains(\"Already up to date\"), \"{output}\");","+    assert!(output.contains(DECIDED_FROM_RECORDS), \"{output}\");","+    assert!(!output.contains(READ_PROJECTS_SPAN), \"{output}\");","+    drop((root, mock_instance));","+}","+","+/// A state whose records are missing, such as one an older pnpm wrote, gets","+/// them from the first check that reads the manifests.","+#[test]","+fn a_check_on_the_files_records_missing_manifest_records() {","+    let CommandTempCwd {","+        pacquet,","+        root,","+        workspace,","+        npmrc_info,","+        ..","+    } = CommandTempCwd::init().add_mocked_registry();","+    let AddMockedRegistry { mock_instance, .. } = npmrc_info;","+    write_workspace(&workspace);","+    pacquet","+        .with_env(\"PNPM_CONFIG_REGISTRY\", mock_instance.url())","+        .with_arg(\"install\")","+        .assert()","+        .success();","+    remove_manifest_records(&workspace);","+    wait_past_whole_second_rounding(&workspace);","+","+    let from_files = traced_install(&workspace, mock_instance.url());","+    let from_records = traced_install(&workspace, mock_instance.url());","+","+    assert!(!from_files.contains(DECIDED_FROM_RECORDS), \"{from_files}\");","+    assert!(from_records.contains(DECIDED_FROM_RECORDS), \"{from_records}\");","+    drop((root, mock_instance));","+}","+","+/// An edit the lockfile still satisfies leaves the install up to date, but","+/// the edited manifest has to be read to tell.","+#[test]","+fn an_edited_manifest_is_read_again() {","+    let CommandTempCwd {","+        pacquet,","+        root,","+        workspace,","+        npmrc_info,","+        ..","+    } = CommandTempCwd::init().add_mocked_registry();","+    let AddMockedRegistry { mock_instance, .. } = npmrc_info;","+    write_workspace(&workspace);","+    pacquet","+        .with_env(\"PNPM_CONFIG_REGISTRY\", mock_instance.url())","+        .with_arg(\"install\")","+        .assert()","+        .success();","+    fs::write(","+        workspace.join(\"packages/b/package.json\"),","+        serde_json::json!({","+            \"name\": \"b\",","+            \"version\": \"1.0.0\",","+            \"description\": \"edited\",","+            \"bin\": { \"b\": \"cli.js\" },","+        })","+        .to_string(),","+    )","+    .expect(\"edit packages/b/package.json\");","+","+    let output = traced_install(&workspace, mock_instance.url());","+","+    assert!(output.contains(\"Already up to date\"), \"{output}\");","+    assert!(!output.contains(DECIDED_FROM_RECORDS), \"{output}\");","+    drop((root, mock_instance));","+}","+","+#[test]","+fn a_new_project_is_read_and_installed() {","+    let CommandTempCwd {","+        pacquet,","+        root,","+        workspace,","+        npmrc_info,","+        ..","+    } = CommandTempCwd::init().add_mocked_registry();","+    let AddMockedRegistry { mock_instance, .. } = npmrc_info;","+    write_workspace(&workspace);","+    pacquet","+        .with_env(\"PNPM_CONFIG_REGISTRY\", mock_instance.url())","+        .with_arg(\"install\")","+        .assert()","+        .success();","+    fs::write(","+        workspace.join(\"packages/no-project/package.json\"),","+        serde_json::json!({ \"name\": \"c\", \"version\": \"1.0.0\", \"dependencies\": { \"b\": \"workspace:*\" } })","+            .to_string(),","+    )","+    .expect(\"write packages/no-project/package.json\");","+","+    let output = traced_install(&workspace, mock_instance.url());","+","+    assert!(!output.contains(DECIDED_FROM_RECORDS), \"{output}\");","+    assert!(workspace.join(\"packages/no-project/node_modules/b\").exists(), \"{output}\");","+    drop((root, mock_instance));","+}","+","+/// The records stand in for the dependencies the link check reads, so a","+/// removed link of an unchanged project is still found.","+#[test]","+fn a_removed_workspace_link_is_relinked() {","+    let CommandTempCwd {","+        pacquet,","+        root,","+        workspace,","+        npmrc_info,","+        ..","+    } = CommandTempCwd::init().add_mocked_registry();","+    let AddMockedRegistry { mock_instance, .. } = npmrc_info;","+    write_workspace(&workspace);","+    pacquet","+        .with_env(\"PNPM_CONFIG_REGISTRY\", mock_instance.url())","+        .with_arg(\"install\")","+        .assert()","+        .success();","+    trust_recorded_stats(&workspace, mock_instance.url());","+    let link = workspace.join(\"packages/a/node_modules/b\");","+    pnpm_fs::remove_dirent(&link).expect(\"remove the workspace link\");","+","+    let output = traced_install(&workspace, mock_instance.url());","+","+    assert!(!output.contains(DECIDED_FROM_RECORDS), \"{output}\");","+    assert!(output.contains(\"the recorded manifests cannot decide\"), \"{output}\");","+    assert!(output.contains(\"a direct dependency link is missing\"), \"{output}\");","+    assert!(link.exists(), \"{output}\");","+    drop((root, mock_instance));","+}","+","+/// Strip the manifest records from the workspace state, as an older pnpm","+/// would have written it.","+fn remove_manifest_records(workspace: &Path) {","+    let state_path = workspace.join(\"node_modules/.pnpm-workspace-state-v1.json\");","+    let mut state: serde_json::Value =","+        serde_json::from_str(&fs::read_to_string(&state_path).expect(\"read the state\"))","+            .expect(\"parse the state\");","+    state[\"validation\"]","+        .as_object_mut()","+        .expect(\"a validation record\")","+        .remove(\"manifestFiles\")","+        .expect(\"manifest records\");","+    fs::write(&state_path, state.to_string()).expect(\"write the state\");","+}","+","+fn state_text(workspace: &Path) -> String {","+    fs::read_to_string(workspace.join(\"node_modules/.pnpm-workspace-state-v1.json\"))","+        .expect(\"read the state\")","+}","+","+/// A record of a manifest dated in the future is never trusted, so writing it","+/// would only repeat the write on the next run.","+#[test]","+fn a_future_dated_manifest_does_not_rewrite_the_state() {","+    let CommandTempCwd {","+        pacquet,","+        root,","+        workspace,","+        npmrc_info,","+        ..","+    } = CommandTempCwd::init().add_mocked_registry();","+    let AddMockedRegistry { mock_instance, .. } = npmrc_info;","+    write_workspace(&workspace);","+    pacquet","+        .with_env(\"PNPM_CONFIG_REGISTRY\", mock_instance.url())","+        .with_arg(\"install\")","+        .assert()","+        .success();","+    pnpm_testing_utils::fs::set_mtime(","+        &workspace.join(\"packages/b/package.json\"),","+        std::time::SystemTime::now() + std::time::Duration::from_hours(1),","+    );","+    let before = state_text(&workspace);","+","+    let output = traced_install(&workspace, mock_instance.url());","+","+    assert!(output.contains(\"Already up to date\"), \"{output}\");","+    assert_eq!(state_text(&workspace), before);","+    drop((root, mock_instance));","+}","+","+/// The run gate leaves inputs such as local file dependencies unchecked, so","+/// only an install refreshes the manifest records.","+#[test]","+fn the_run_gate_leaves_missing_records_to_the_install() {","+    let CommandTempCwd {","+        pacquet,","+        root,","+        workspace,","+        npmrc_info,","+        ..","+    } = CommandTempCwd::init().add_mocked_registry();","+    let AddMockedRegistry { mock_instance, .. } = npmrc_info;","+    write_workspace(&workspace);","+    let workspace_yaml = workspace.join(\"pnpm-workspace.yaml\");","+    let mut yaml = fs::read_to_string(&workspace_yaml).expect(\"read pnpm-workspace.yaml\");","+    yaml.push_str(\"verifyDepsBeforeRun: install\\n\");","+    fs::write(&workspace_yaml, yaml).expect(\"write pnpm-workspace.yaml\");","+    fs::write(","+        workspace.join(\"package.json\"),","+        serde_json::json!({ \"name\": \"root\", \"private\": true, \"scripts\": { \"noop\": \"node -e 0\" } })","+            .to_string(),","+    )","+    .expect(\"write package.json\");","+    pacquet","+        .with_env(\"PNPM_CONFIG_REGISTRY\", mock_instance.url())","+        .with_arg(\"install\")","+        .assert()","+        .success();","+    remove_manifest_records(&workspace);","+","+    pacquet_in(&workspace)","+        .with_env(\"PNPM_CONFIG_REGISTRY\", mock_instance.url())","+        .with_args([\"run\", \"noop\"])","+        .assert()","+        .success();","+    assert!(!state_text(&workspace).contains(\"manifestFiles\"), \"the run gate refreshed records\");","+    wait_past_whole_second_rounding(&workspace);","+","+    let from_files = traced_install(&workspace, mock_instance.url());","+    let from_records = traced_install(&workspace, mock_instance.url());","+    assert!(!from_files.contains(DECIDED_FROM_RECORDS), \"{from_files}\");","+    assert!(from_records.contains(DECIDED_FROM_RECORDS), \"{from_records}\");","+    drop((root, mock_instance));","+}"],"additions":338,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpm/crates/package-manager/src/install/lifecycle.rs","lines":["@@ -28,11 +28,23 @@ pub(super) fn load_workspace_projects(","     ignored_directories: &[std::path::PathBuf],"," ) -> Result<Option<Vec<pnpm_workspace::Project>>, pnpm_workspace::FindWorkspaceProjectsError> {","     let Some(manifest) = workspace_manifest else { return Ok(None) };","-    let opts = pnpm_workspace::FindWorkspaceProjectsOpts {","-        patterns: Some(pnpm_workspace::workspace_package_patterns(manifest)),","+    pnpm_workspace::find_workspace_projects(","+        workspace_root,","+        &workspace_projects_opts(manifest, ignored_directories),","+    )","+    .map(Some)","+}","+","+/// How [`load_workspace_projects`] discovers the projects of the workspace","+/// `workspace_manifest` declares.","+pub(super) fn workspace_projects_opts(","+    workspace_manifest: &pnpm_workspace::WorkspaceManifest,","+    ignored_directories: &[std::path::PathBuf],","+) -> pnpm_workspace::FindWorkspaceProjectsOpts {","+    pnpm_workspace::FindWorkspaceProjectsOpts {","+        patterns: Some(pnpm_workspace::workspace_package_patterns(workspace_manifest)),","         ignored_directories: ignored_directories.to_vec(),","-    };","-    pnpm_workspace::find_workspace_projects(workspace_root, &opts).map(Some)","+    }"," }"," "," /// [`Config::extra_env_with_node_options`] plus the `NODE_OPTIONS` entry for"],"additions":16,"deletions":4,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpm/crates/package-manager/src/install/workspace_state.rs","lines":["@@ -11,6 +11,10 @@ mod projects;"," "," mod discovery;"," ","+mod from_files;","+","+mod stand_ins;","+"," mod nothing_to_install;"," "," mod write;","@@ -112,28 +116,23 @@ pub fn install_already_up_to_date(","     let (workspace_manifest, catalogs) =","         fast_path_workspace_context(check.config, workspace_dir_opt.as_deref())","             .ok_or(\"the workspace manifest or its catalogs cannot be read\")?;","-    let workspace_projects =","-        discover_fast_path_projects(check.config, workspace_root, workspace_manifest.as_ref())?;","-    let project_manifests =","-        build_project_manifests_list(check.manifest, workspace_projects.as_deref());","     let lockfile = lazy_wanted_lockfile(check.config, &lockfile_root);","-    check_fast_path_repeat_install(","-        check,","-        FastPathInputs {","-            state_root,","-            lockfile_root: &lockfile_root,","-            state,","-            project_manifests: &project_manifests,","-            is_workspace_install: workspace_manifest.is_some(),","-            lockfile: &lockfile,","-            catalogs: &catalogs,","-        },","-    )?;","+    let context = FastPathContext {","+        state_root,","+        lockfile_root: &lockfile_root,","+        workspace_root,","+        workspace_manifest: workspace_manifest.as_ref(),","+        lockfile: &lockfile,","+        catalogs: &catalogs,","+    };","+    let project_count = match stand_ins::check_from_records(check, &context, &state) {","+        stand_ins::RecordsCheck::UpToDate(project_count) => Some(project_count),","+        stand_ins::RecordsCheck::Undecided(listed) => {","+            from_files::check_from_files(check, &context, &state, listed)?","+        }","+    };","     register_fast_path_workspace(check.config, &lockfile_root)?;","-    Ok(UpToDateWorkspace {","-        root: state_root.to_path_buf(),","-        project_count: workspace_projects.as_ref().map(Vec::len),","-    })","+    Ok(UpToDateWorkspace { root: state_root.to_path_buf(), project_count })"," }"," "," fn load_fast_path_state(","@@ -156,46 +155,47 @@ fn load_fast_path_state(","         .ok_or(\"no workspace state on disk\")"," }"," ","-/// [`load_workspace_projects`] inside the `discover_workspace_projects`","-/// span, skipping the pnpm-managed directories.","-fn discover_fast_path_projects(","-    config: &Config,","-    workspace_root: &Path,","-    workspace_manifest: Option<&pnpm_workspace::WorkspaceManifest>,","-) -> Result<Option<Vec<pnpm_workspace::Project>>, &'static str> {","-    let _span =","-        tracing::debug_span!(target: \"pacquet::install\", \"discover_workspace_projects\").entered();","-    load_workspace_projects(workspace_root, workspace_manifest, &config.managed_directories())","-        .map_err(|_| \"the workspace projects cannot be listed\")","-}","-","-/// What [`install_already_up_to_date`] has established about the project","-/// tree by the time it checks the repeat install.","-struct FastPathInputs<'a> {","+/// What [`install_already_up_to_date`] has established about the workspace","+/// before it reads any project.","+struct FastPathContext<'a> {","     state_root: &'a Path,","     lockfile_root: &'a Path,","-    state: WorkspaceState,","-    project_manifests: &'a [(PathBuf, &'a PackageManifest)],","-    is_workspace_install: bool,","+    workspace_root: &'a Path,","+    /// `None` when no `pnpm-workspace.yaml` drives the install.","+    workspace_manifest: Option<&'a pnpm_workspace::WorkspaceManifest>,","     lockfile: &'a LazyLockfile,","     catalogs: &'a Catalogs,"," }"," ","+/// The projects one repeat-install check covers.","+#[derive(Clone, Copy)]","+struct FastPathProjects<'a> {","+    state: &'a WorkspaceState,","+    manifests: &'a [(PathBuf, &'a PackageManifest)],","+    /// See [`crate::DeclaredManifests::with_stand_ins`].","+    recorded_digests: Option<&'a std::collections::HashMap<PathBuf, String>>,","+}","+"," /// [`check_optimistic_repeat_install_with_state`] inside the"," /// `check_repeat_install` span, with a skip surfaced as the fast path's reason."," fn check_fast_path_repeat_install(","     check: &UpToDateFastPathCheck<'_>,","-    inputs: FastPathInputs<'_>,","+    context: &FastPathContext<'_>,","+    projects: FastPathProjects<'_>,"," ) -> Result<(), &'static str> {","     let _span = tracing::debug_span!(target: \"pacquet::install\", \"check_repeat_install\").entered();","+    let project_manifests = match projects.recorded_digests {","+        Some(digests) => crate::DeclaredManifests::with_stand_ins(projects.manifests, digests),","+        None => crate::DeclaredManifests::new(projects.manifests),","+    };","     let decision = check_optimistic_repeat_install_with_state(","         &OptimisticRepeatInstallCheck {","-            workspace_root: inputs.state_root,","+            workspace_root: context.state_root,","             config: check.config,","-            project_manifests: crate::DeclaredManifests::new(inputs.project_manifests),","-            is_workspace_install: inputs.is_workspace_install,","-            lockfile: MaybeLazyLockfile::Lazy(inputs.lockfile),","-            catalogs: inputs.catalogs,","+            project_manifests,","+            is_workspace_install: context.workspace_manifest.is_some(),","+            lockfile: MaybeLazyLockfile::Lazy(context.lockfile),","+            catalogs: context.catalogs,","             layout: crate::RepeatInstallLayout {","                 node_linker: check.node_linker,","                 included: super::included_dependencies(&check.dependency_groups),","@@ -203,14 +203,14 @@ fn check_fast_path_repeat_install(","             },","             manifests: crate::RepeatInstallManifests::ON_DISK,","         },","-        inputs.state,","+        projects.state,","         Scope::Workspace,","     );","     match decision {","         OptimisticRepeatInstallDecision::UpToDate => super::run::gvs_build_markers_complete(","             check.config,","-            MaybeLazyLockfile::Lazy(inputs.lockfile),","-            inputs.lockfile_root,","+            MaybeLazyLockfile::Lazy(context.lockfile),","+            context.lockfile_root,","             super::effective_node_version(check.config, check.manifest).as_deref(),","         ),","         OptimisticRepeatInstallDecision::Skipped { reason } => Err(reason),"],"additions":48,"deletions":48,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpm/crates/package-manager/src/install/workspace_state/from_files.rs","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,47 @@","+//! The fast path's check on the manifest files, which discovery reads.","+","+use super::{","+    Config, FastPathContext, FastPathProjects, UpToDateFastPathCheck, WorkspaceState,","+    build_project_manifests_list, check_fast_path_repeat_install, load_workspace_projects,","+};","+","+/// The repeat-install check on the manifests discovery reads, returning the","+/// number of workspace projects. Discovery reads the projects `listed`","+/// names, when the caller already listed them.","+pub(super) fn check_from_files(","+    check: &UpToDateFastPathCheck<'_>,","+    context: &FastPathContext<'_>,","+    state: &WorkspaceState,","+    listed: Option<Vec<pnpm_workspace::ProjectManifestPaths>>,","+) -> Result<Option<usize>, &'static str> {","+    let workspace_projects = discover_fast_path_projects(check.config, context, listed)?;","+    let project_manifests =","+        build_project_manifests_list(check.manifest, workspace_projects.as_deref());","+    check_fast_path_repeat_install(","+        check,","+        context,","+        FastPathProjects { state, manifests: &project_manifests, recorded_digests: None },","+    )?;","+    Ok(workspace_projects.as_ref().map(Vec::len))","+}","+","+/// [`load_workspace_projects`] inside the `discover_workspace_projects`","+/// span, skipping the pnpm-managed directories, or the read of the projects","+/// `listed` names.","+fn discover_fast_path_projects(","+    config: &Config,","+    context: &FastPathContext<'_>,","+    listed: Option<Vec<pnpm_workspace::ProjectManifestPaths>>,","+) -> Result<Option<Vec<pnpm_workspace::Project>>, &'static str> {","+    let _span =","+        tracing::debug_span!(target: \"pacquet::install\", \"discover_workspace_projects\").entered();","+    let discovered = match listed {","+        Some(listed) => pnpm_workspace::read_workspace_projects(listed).map(Some),","+        None => load_workspace_projects(","+            context.workspace_root,","+            context.workspace_manifest,","+            &config.managed_directories(),","+        ),","+    };","+    discovered.map_err(|_| \"the workspace projects cannot be listed\")","+}"],"additions":47,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpm/crates/package-manager/src/install/workspace_state/stand_ins.rs","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,96 @@","+//! The fast path's first attempt: the repeat-install check on manifests","+//! rebuilt from the last validation's records, before discovery reads any","+//! project manifest.","+","+use super::{","+    FastPathContext, FastPathProjects, PackageManifest, PathBuf, UpToDateFastPathCheck,","+    WorkspaceState, build_project_manifests_list, check_fast_path_repeat_install,","+};","+use crate::optimistic_repeat_install::validation::{ManifestStandIns, manifest_stand_ins};","+use pnpm_workspace::ProjectManifestPaths;","+use std::collections::HashMap;","+","+/// What the check on the stand-ins decided.","+pub(super) enum RecordsCheck {","+    /// The install is up to date. Holds the number of workspace projects.","+    UpToDate(usize),","+    /// The check on the files decides. Holds the listing the attempt made,","+    /// for that check to read.","+    Undecided(Option<Vec<ProjectManifestPaths>>),","+}","+","+/// The repeat-install check on the stand-ins. It leaves the decision to the","+/// check on the files when no workspace manifest drives the install, the","+/// state has no manifest records, a project's manifest may have changed","+/// since the last validation, or the check would refresh the state.","+pub(super) fn check_from_records(","+    check: &UpToDateFastPathCheck<'_>,","+    context: &FastPathContext<'_>,","+    state: &WorkspaceState,","+) -> RecordsCheck {","+    let has_records = state.validation","+        .as_ref()","+        .is_some_and(|validation| !validation.manifest_files.is_empty());","+    if !has_records {","+        return RecordsCheck::Undecided(None);","+    }","+    let Some(listed) = list_projects(check, context) else {","+        return RecordsCheck::Undecided(None);","+    };","+    let Some(stand_ins) = state.validation","+        .as_ref()","+        .and_then(|validation| manifest_stand_ins(context.state_root, validation, &listed))","+    else {","+        return RecordsCheck::Undecided(Some(listed));","+    };","+    let project_manifests = build_project_manifests_list(check.manifest, Some(&stand_ins.projects));","+    let recorded_digests = stand_in_digests(&project_manifests, &stand_ins, check.manifest);","+    let checked = check_fast_path_repeat_install(","+        check,","+        context,","+        FastPathProjects {","+            state,","+            manifests: &project_manifests,","+            recorded_digests: Some(&recorded_digests),","+        },","+    );","+    if let Err(reason) = checked {","+        tracing::debug!(target: \"pacquet::install\", reason, \"the recorded manifests cannot decide\");","+        return RecordsCheck::Undecided(Some(listed));","+    }","+    tracing::debug!(target: \"pacquet::install\", \"the recorded manifests decided the install\");","+    RecordsCheck::UpToDate(stand_ins.projects.len())","+}","+","+/// [`pnpm_workspace::find_workspace_project_manifests`] for the workspace","+/// manifest, inside the `list_workspace_projects` span.","+fn list_projects(","+    check: &UpToDateFastPathCheck<'_>,","+    context: &FastPathContext<'_>,","+) -> Option<Vec<ProjectManifestPaths>> {","+    let _span =","+        tracing::debug_span!(target: \"pacquet::install\", \"list_workspace_projects\").entered();","+    let opts = super::super::lifecycle::workspace_projects_opts(","+        context.workspace_manifest?,","+        &check.config.managed_directories(),","+    );","+    pnpm_workspace::find_workspace_project_manifests(context.workspace_root, &opts).ok()","+}","+","+/// The recorded digests of the stand-ins `project_manifests` holds.","+/// [`build_project_manifests_list`] puts the active project's manifest,","+/// which the command read from disk, in place of its stand-in.","+fn stand_in_digests(","+    project_manifests: &[(PathBuf, &PackageManifest)],","+    stand_ins: &ManifestStandIns,","+    active_manifest: &PackageManifest,","+) -> HashMap<PathBuf, String> {","+    project_manifests","+        .iter()","+        .filter(|(_, manifest)| !std::ptr::eq(*manifest, active_manifest))","+        .filter_map(|(root_dir, _)| {","+            let digest = stand_ins.digests.get(root_dir)?;","+            Some((root_dir.clone(), digest.clone()))","+        })","+        .collect()","+}"],"additions":96,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpm/crates/package-manager/src/optimistic_repeat_install.rs","lines":["@@ -183,22 +183,23 @@ pub(crate) fn check_optimistic_repeat_install_in(","     let Ok(Some(state)) = load_workspace_state(check.workspace_root) else {","         return Decision::Skipped { reason: \"no workspace state on disk\" };","     };","-    check_optimistic_repeat_install_with_state(check, state, scope)","+    check_optimistic_repeat_install_with_state(check, &state, scope)"," }"," "," pub(crate) fn check_optimistic_repeat_install_with_state(","     check: &OptimisticRepeatInstallCheck<'_>,","-    state: WorkspaceState,","+    state: &WorkspaceState,","     scope: Scope<'_>,"," ) -> Decision {","-    let (state, moved) = relocation::relocated_state(","-        &state,","+    let relocated = relocation::relocated_state(","+        state,","         check.workspace_root,","         check.project_manifests.as_